# .cbmignore — codebase-graph (codebase-memory MCP) ignore rules.
# gitignore-style syntax, one pattern per line. Merged with .gitignore at index time.
# Scope: files that DON'T need indexing AND that agents will never need to interact with.
# Default ignores (node_modules, dist, out, build, coverage, .git, *.min.js, images, etc.)
# are already hardcoded in the indexer — do NOT duplicate them here.
#
# Do NOT add agent-facing content here: src/**, roadmap/** (HANDOFF, waves, decisions),
# .claude/**, tests, hook scripts, issues/**, README files. Agents read those.

# Vendored @xterm/addon-webgl source kept in-tree for patch-package reference.
# These are before/after snapshots of a third-party library, not project source.
# Indexing them injected ~1,032 third-party symbols (864 Function + 146 Method +
# 22 Class) into the graph as fake project hits. patches/README.md stays indexed
# (it explains the patch — agent-relevant). Pattern matches the *.original.* / *.patched.*
# naming convention so future vendored patches are covered automatically.
patches/*.original.*
patches/*.patched.*

# Generated third-party license aggregation (7,000+ lines, zero symbols).
# Never authored or read by agents during code work.
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
